{
  "assembly_notes": "Single source (SOURCES=1): an expandable hanging-file organizer, decomposed into four independent structural axes instead of one monolithic family slot. leaf_top owns the leaf's top hardware, gusset_style the per-gap connective fold, cover_build the rigid end cover construction and closure the moving-end closure hardware (0 or 1 revolute DOF). All 3x3x3x3 = 81 combinations build: the accordion host, the leaf/cover panels and the retention tapes (source _add_side_attachment, model.py:L94-L114) are shared and re-derived from one parameter DAG, so no compatibility gate is needed. Interior leaves are parented to the fixed end board as a mimic star (leaf i mimics the driver with multiplier i+1) so the source's uniform accordion expansion is preserved while every file_leaf shares one end_board->file_leaf prismatic relation; the moving cover rides the same star as gap N+1. divider_count is a structural multiplicity applied to leaf_top: each N adds one file_leaf part, one accordion gap joint, one fold set and one retention tape pair, and re-derives the accordion origins, the gusset band and the moving cover placement. Bindings are left empty because the accordion provider is the shared fixed end-cover host rather than a per-candidate interface; the derivations are recorded here instead: the gusset band is derived as [-pitch + prev_thickness/2 + trim_bulge + clear, -own_thickness/2 + anchor] and the retention tape reach as gap_travel_m + 4 mm, so every candidate stays in support contact at the compressed pose and never interpenetrates at any pose. depth_m, leaf_height_m, compressed_pitch_m and gap_travel_m are honest continuous parameters and do not inflate core/raw.",
